+# v5 NDU-DMGP: independent decoded-output × realized-cost gate
+
+Status: **RESEARCH_ONLY / SHADOW_ONLY / DENY_ALL / HOLD_NO_GO**.  Additive extension to
+`research/ndu-v5-factorial-learning-20261023` at exact source head
+`d98229a03150fb598082c32b206bc22aeb6695ce` (PR #3522). Original frozen
+`factorial.py`, frozen `development-report.json`, `SOURCE_LOCK.json`,
+`AUDIT_LOCK.json`, independently scored output ledger and existing code remain
+unchanged. Neither scientific preregistration nor external model authorization is
+inferred by this addition.
+
+## Specific observed gap
+
+A shared per-episode budget **cap of 7 synthetic units** does not identify the
+quality-to-cost frontier if executed costs differ. On the frozen three seeds,
+the supervised-training static versus dynamic contrasts are:
+
+| Seed | External decoded mean loss static -> dynamic | Executed toy cost static -> dynamic | Refine activation |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 17 | 1.1953125 -> 0.78515625 | 4 -> 4.298828125 | 0 |
+| 29 | 0.1328125 -> 0.3359375 | 7 -> 4.7265625 | 0 |
+| 43 | 1.1796875 -> 0.861328125 | 4 -> 4.263671875 | 0 |
+
+Seed 29 is a retained *harm in output quality*, not a failed test to tune away.
+No supervised arm is equal-realized-cost within 0.05 toy unit, and the observed
+control change is overwhelmingly QUERY rather than a text/audio/image/video
+refinement. v5 currently tests a **one-action**, not full multistep generator
+portfolio, and only 2x2 training-by-inference contrasts, not A0-A5.
+
+## Executable reproducible gate
+
+`cost_parity_gate.py` generates all four raw decoded synthetic outputs for
+both training methods and both inference methods on the same test source group,
+re-scores each with the separately maintained `independent_observer.observe`,
+then validates exactly one source × arm row, common input digest, source truth,
+complete roster, admissible action, *executed* modeled cost and observed decoded
+loss. It reports paired static-minus-dynamic loss and dynamic-minus-static
+executed cost **per seed and training**, without treating four outputs as four
+independent sampling units.
+
+`test_cost_parity_gate.py` rejects forged scores, costs, action names, incomplete
+or repeated source/arm rows, cross-arm input changes, malformed media shapes,
+unknown train split, invalid numeric thresholds and unsupported census. An
+integration test exercises the real v5 `factorial` and `independent_observer`
+imports; the frozen report test preserves the seed-29 negative result and zero
+modality refinements. Tests use stdlib only.
+
+Use from the `v5` directory:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -p 'test_*.py' -v
+python3 -m compileall -q cost_parity_gate.py test_cost_parity_gate.py
+python3 cost_parity_gate.py > /tmp/hepta-v5-paired-cost-audit.json
+```
+
+The full run replays the **already used development** seed set (17,29,43), 768
+train + 256 dev + 512 test per seed. The output is a diagnostic, *not* a new
+prospective or physically attested confirmation experiment. The frozen v5
+independent observer already has its own source/audit locks, and this additive
+gate cannot substitute a second external institution, a hardware meter, or new
+natural source acquisition.
+
+The bounded-loss Hoeffding LCB is a deliberately conservative diagnostic with
+Bonferroni for six within-seed/training comparisons. Synthetic source worlds
+are the declared sampling units. It does not make a statistical claim about
+natural human task distributions or cross-seed scientific replication.
+
+## Exact blocker semantics (OPEN unless independent evidence exists)
+
+| Blocker | Required real-world close criterion |
+| --- | --- |
+| B1 NDU truth/reward | Registered fixed external objective; independent authentic source and signed observer, held-out groups, actual cost ledger, no Actor/Critic self-labelling |
+| B2 Cross-modal consistency | Actual forward/reverse audio-visual-text-image perception with event/entity/time/sync checks on held-out natural media |
+| B3 Conditional covariance | Paired joint real decoder-intervention trajectories, support/identifiability and PSD/low-rank/shrinkage plus deterministic fallback |
+| B4 Efficiency | Matched **realized** quality/cost, host CPU/GPU/RSS/energy/end-to-end p95/p99, controller overhead and equal-budget strong baselines |
+| B5 Stability | Frozen objective and independent Critic/Actor revisions, explicit trust region, signed next-snapshot candidate and future-window/retention/OOD results |
+| B6 Global credit | Independently supported source-level counterfactual local advantages, coalition residuals and history-vs-state sufficiency/Markov closure on real Cell/Circuit owners |
+
+Additional necessary bridge: A0-A5's qualified six-arm experiment must be
+source/version-integrated with v5's distinct 2x2 train/control experiment before
+any single combined superiority assertion. A static A1 comparator, a learned
+Top-k/MoE comparator, myopic NDU, covariance NDU and full dynamic NDU should
+all use the same frozen backbone/decoder/source groups/registered resource and
+observer revisions. Require source-level evidence first, actual host and
+independent acceptance later. A5<=A1 in existing synthetic A0-A5 reference
+must remain visible; do not relabel that negative result as a victory.
+
+All production capability flags remain false.  No current-run parameter
+replacement, authority, final-use, runtime dispatch, model promotion, or deployment
+is issued by this audit or its scores.
